       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and overdose-type toxicity. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg once daily**, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated to 10 mg.\n- **2.5 mg once daily**, which is often used for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 30 mg is intentional, for example as part of a specialist-directed regimen, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I can then enter it with that note. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
